// Pull request author: veeramani-sl-12207
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Executable Created In AOMEI Backupper Tmphtml Directory
// Sigma ID: d18188bb-42c7-4c37-8a50-b3c865c5508d
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Veeramani
// Date: 2026-08-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: initial-access, T1195.002, stealth
// Description: Detects a file creation event for any executable inside the "tmphtml" staging directory beneath
//   the AOMEI Backupper installation path, where the creating process is Backupper.exe. The
//   application stages popup resources here before relocating them to html\; a genuine promotional
//   bundle contains no executables, so an .exe written to this path indicates a tampered bundle.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.manageengine.com/threat-analysis-lab/aomei-backupper-supply-chain-compromise.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/61757c593d21d62428a54bb9b9191a1de0e0ca82/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_aomei_backupper_susp_exe_in_tmphtml.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\AOMEI\\AOMEI Backupper\\" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\Backupper.exe") and ((FolderPath contains "\\AOMEI\\AOMEI Backupper\\" and FolderPath contains "\\tmphtml\\") and FolderPath endswith ".exe")
